// Where an empty list literal is allowed. idc.py hands an expected type down
// one level, from four places only: a typed declaration, an assignment to a
// known variable, the value of an index-assignment, and push's second
// argument. The AST has no parent links, so the same question is asked
// backwards -- does any node hand THIS node a list type? A whole-store scan
// per literal is affordable because empty literals are rare and this only
// runs once, at check time.

arr_ok(int id) {
  int i = 0;
  int ok = 0;
  while(i < len((import nkind))) {
    ok = arr_ok_at(i, id, ok);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return int ok;
